-- title:
--   Raynaud dévissage for split étale p-torsion Hopf algebras
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative local ring, $K$ a perfect field with an $R$-algebra structure, $p$ a prime and $N,n$ natural numbers. Assume the Teichmüller data hypothesis `hT`: for every $s$ with $0<s\le N$ and every finite field $F$ with $|F|=p^{s}$, the element $p^{s}-1$ is a unit of $R$ and there are a group homomorphism $\chi\colon F^{\times}\to R^{\times}$ and a ring homomorphism $\iota\colon F\to \mathrm{ResidueField}(R)$ with $\mathrm{residue}_R(\chi(l))=\iota(l)$ for all $l\in F^{\times}$. Let $A$ be a commutative ring which is a cocommutative Hopf algebra over $K$, finite as a $K$-module, such that the set of $K$-algebra maps $A\to\overline K$, equipped with the convolution monoid structure `WithConv`, is finite; assume `hev`, that the algebra map $\overline K\otimes_K A\to \overline K^{\,V}$ induced by the structure map and by evaluation at the points $\nu\in V:=\mathrm{WithConv}(A\to_{\mathrm{alg}}\overline K)$ is bijective; assume $\#V\le p^{N}$ and $\nu^{p^{n}}=1$ for all $\nu\in V$. Let $L$ be a finite Galois intermediate field of $\overline K/K$ through which all points factor, i.e. $\nu(a)\in L$ for every point $\nu$ and $a\in A$, and suppose $\mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ has a normal $p$-subgroup $P$ containing all commutators $a^{-1}b^{-1}ab$. Then [`HopfAlgebra.HasFVectDevissage R K p A`](def/HopfAlgebra_HasFVectDevissage.html#L10) holds: $A$ lies in the inductively defined class generated by the Hopf algebras of $K$-rank $1$ and closed under the following step — $A$ (finite, cocommutative) admits a surjective $K$-bialgebra map $\pi\colon A\to\bar A$ onto a finite cocommutative Hopf algebra $\bar A$ in the class, together with $r\ge 1$, a finite field $F$ with $|F|=p^{r}$, a unit $p^{r}-1$ of $R$ and Teichmüller data $(\chi,\iota)$ for $F$ as above, such that the Hopf kernel $\mathrm{hopfKer}\,\pi$ (the equalizer of the coaction of $\pi$ and $A\to A\otimes_K\bar A$) has $K$-rank $p^{r}$ and carries an $F$-vector space structure `FVectStructure`, namely an action of $F$ by $K$-bialgebra endomorphisms which is multiplicative ($\mathrm{act}\,1=\mathrm{id}$, $\mathrm{act}(ab)=\mathrm{act}\,a\circ\mathrm{act}\,b$) and additive for the convolution product ($\mathrm{act}\,0=1$, $\mathrm{act}(a+b)=\mathrm{act}\,a\cdot\mathrm{act}\,b$ in the convolution monoid).
--
--   This is Raynaud's dévissage of a finite commutative group scheme of type $(p,\dots,p)$ into successive $F$-vector space extensions (Schémas en groupes de type $(p,\dots,p)$, §3.2), in the dual Hopf-algebra formulation and in the situation where the base field is perfect and the points are already rational over a Galois extension with $p$-group-by-abelian Galois group. It is used by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_faithfullyFlat_hasFVectDevissage_baseChange_of_pow_eq_one`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_faithfullyFlat_hasFVectDevissage_baseChange_of_pow_eq_one), where the required base change enlarging $K$ and $R$ is produced first.
